course: dictionary
lesson: 15280
title: Made to look real
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Simulated means made to look or feel real, but not real. It is an imitation. Look for the clues in the sentence: «The class practised a fire drill with simulated smoke.» The smoke is not real fire smoke, but it looks like it, so the children can practise safely.
explain: Simulated can also mean created by a computer to show what would happen in real life. «The pilot trained in a computer-simulated flight.» Nobody left the ground, but the computer copied a real flight. Ask yourself: what real thing is this copying?
explain: Simulated is also the past form of the verb simulate, which means to pretend. «She simulated surprise when she opened the present.» She was not really surprised; she acted surprised. Check the sentence: does the word mean real, or pretend? Here it means pretend.
fact: Simulated means made to look or feel real, but not real.
fact: «A simulated emergency» is a practice run, so people learn what to do.
fact: «Computer-simulated» means a computer model shows what would happen in real life.
fact: Simulate is a verb; simulated is its past form, meaning pretended, as in «She simulated surprise».
fact: «Simulated fur» looks like real fur, but it is an imitation.
exercise: «The class practised a fire drill with simulated smoke.» What does simulated mean here? | *Made to look real, but not real | Real smoke from a bonfire | Blown away by the wind | Very hot and dangerous
exercise: Ravi says the pilots trained in a «computer-simulated flight». What does this mean? | A real plane flight over the sea | A flight of birds | A flight of stairs | *A flight copied on a computer, so nobody leaves the ground
exercise: «She simulated surprise when she opened the present.» What does simulated mean here? | Wrapped the present again | Was truly surprised | Opened the present slowly | *Pretended to be surprised
test: «The shop sold simulated fur coats.» What does simulated fur mean? | Fur from a famous shop | Fur that is very wet | Real fur from a wild animal | *Fur that looks real but is an imitation
test: In «The doctors ran a simulated emergency», which word tells you the emergency was practice, not real? | emergency | *simulated | ran | doctors
exam: «The room had a simulated sky painted on the ceiling.» Simulated means... | *Made to look like the sky, but not the real sky | Blue because it is raining | Made of glass | Covered with real clouds
